 "text": "\n\n<｜DSML｜function_calls\n\n<｜DSML｜function_callsBased on my biomedical knowledge:\n\nLeptin is an adipokine (hormone produced by fat cells) that is elevated in obesity. It has been shown to activate immune cells including macrophages and neutrophils. Phagocytic NADPH oxidase (NOX2) is an enzyme complex in immune cells that produces reactive oxygen species (ROS). In obesity, there is chronic low-grade inflammation and immune cell activation.\n\nResearch indicates that leptin can stimulate NADPH oxidase activity in phagocytes through various signaling pathways, contributing to oxidative stress and inflammation in obesity. However, the relationship is complex with multiple factors involved.\n\n{\"answer\": \"yes\", \"confidence\": 75}",
